<title>SPAIN: Spain's Bankinter to propose share cancellation.</title>
<headline>Spain's Bankinter to propose share cancellation.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Bankinter said on Thursday it would propose cancelling 1.2 percent of its shares, or 252.3 million shares, paying back 120 pesetas per share to shareholders.</p>
<p>Bankinter will discuss the proposal at next shareholders meeting on June 26, a spokesman said.  </p>
<p>On May 27, Bankinter said it would also propose at the shareholders meeting splitting its shares three-for-one, reducing the nominal value of each to 500 pesetas from 1,500.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
